---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const COLLECTOR_CONFIG = `receivers:
  otlp:
    protocols:
      grpc:
        endpoint: 0.0.0.0:4317
      http:
        endpoint: 0.0.0.0:4318

processors:
  batch: {}

exporters:
  otlphttp:
    endpoint: https://api.24observe.com/api/v1/otlp
    compression: gzip
    headers:
      authorization: "Bearer \${env:OBSERVE24_PAT}"

service:
  pipelines:
    logs:
      receivers: [otlp]
      processors: [batch]
      exporters: [otlphttp]
    traces:
      receivers: [otlp]
      processors: [batch]
      exporters: [otlphttp]
    metrics:
      receivers: [otlp]
      processors: [batch]
      exporters: [otlphttp]`;

const SYSLOG_FLUENT_EXTRAS = `# Add to the receivers block:
  syslog/rfc5424:
    tcp:
      listen_address: 0.0.0.0:5414
    protocol: rfc5424
  syslog/rfc3164:
    udp:
      listen_address: 0.0.0.0:5413
    protocol: rfc3164
  fluentforward:
    endpoint: 0.0.0.0:24224

# And widen the logs pipeline:
#   receivers: [otlp, syslog/rfc5424, syslog/rfc3164, fluentforward]`;
---
<Base
  title="OpenTelemetry Collector with 24Observe — gRPC, syslog, and Fluent Bit in one config"
  description="Point the standard OpenTelemetry Collector at 24observe with one config file: OTLP gRPC + HTTP in, authenticated gzip OTLP out. Verified config included."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 820px;">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="bar"></span> Docs · collector</div>
      <h1 class="h1">The standard Collector. One config. Everything flows here.</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top: 24px;">
        24observe works with the stock
        <a href="https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector-contrib">OpenTelemetry Collector (contrib)</a> —
        no custom image, no fork. Drop in the config below and the collector accepts
        telemetry over <b>OTLP/gRPC</b> (the SDK and collector default) and OTLP/HTTP,
        then forwards it to 24observe authenticated and gzip-compressed.
      </p>
      <p>
        Use the collector when your apps export over gRPC, when you don't want the API
        token in every app's environment, or when you have legacy sources (syslog,
        Fluent Bit). If your SDK already exports OTLP/HTTP, you can also target our
        <a href="/docs/logs#opentelemetry-otlphttp">endpoint</a> directly — we accept
        JSON and binary protobuf natively.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 48px;">The config (verified against the live API)</h2>
      <p>Save as <code>config.yaml</code>:</p>
      <pre class="code-block">{COLLECTOR_CONFIG}</pre>
      <p>
        The <code>otlphttp</code> exporter appends <code>/v1/logs</code>,
        <code>/v1/traces</code>, <code>/v1/metrics</code> to the endpoint automatically —
        don't add them yourself. The PAT needs the <code>logs:write</code> scope
        (plus <code>metrics:write</code> if you ship metrics). Mint one with:
      </p>
      <pre class="code-block">{`curl -X POST https://api.24observe.com/api/v1/me/tokens \\
  -H 'Authorization: Bearer obs_<your-existing-admin-token>' \\
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \\
  -d '{ "name": "collector", "scopes": ["logs:write", "metrics:write"] }'`}</pre>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 48px;">Run it (Docker)</h2>
      <pre class="code-block">{`docker run -d --name otelcol \\
  -e OBSERVE24_PAT=obs_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx \\
  -v $(pwd)/config.yaml:/etc/otelcol-contrib/config.yaml:ro \\
  -p 4317:4317 -p 4318:4318 \\
  otel/opentelemetry-collector-contrib:latest`}</pre>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 48px;">Run it (docker compose)</h2>
      <pre class="code-block">{`services:
  otelcol:
    image: otel/opentelemetry-collector-contrib:latest
    environment:
      OBSERVE24_PAT: \${OBSERVE24_PAT}
    volumes:
      - ./config.yaml:/etc/otelcol-contrib/config.yaml:ro
    ports:
      - "4317:4317"
      - "4318:4318"
    restart: unless-stopped`}</pre>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 48px;">Point your apps at it</h2>
      <pre class="code-block">{`OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4317   # gRPC, the default
# That's it — no protocol override, no auth headers in your apps.
# The collector adds the 24observe PAT on the outbound hop.`}</pre>
      <p>
        This is the zero-config path: every official OTel SDK and every existing
        collector deployment exports OTLP/gRPC to <code>localhost:4317</code> by
        default, and this config bridges it to 24observe unchanged.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 48px;">Verify it's flowing</h2>
      <p>
        The collector project ships <code>telemetrygen</code> for exactly this. Send five
        test traces through your collector, then check the Logs view:
      </p>
      <pre class="code-block">{`docker run --rm --network host \\
  ghcr.io/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-collector-contrib/telemetrygen:latest \\
  traces --otlp-endpoint localhost:4317 --otlp-insecure --traces 5

# Then search:  service:telemetrygen        (in the dashboard or via the API)`}</pre>
      <p>
        This whole page is tested exactly as written — collector
        <code>contrib:latest</code>, gRPC in, gzip out — against the live API.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 48px;">Legacy sources: syslog &amp; Fluent Bit</h2>
      <p>
        The contrib image includes receivers for syslog and Fluent Forward; extend
        the same config:
      </p>
      <pre class="code-block">{SYSLOG_FLUENT_EXTRAS}</pre>
      <p>
        Then point rsyslog at <code>@@collector-host:5414</code> (RFC5424/TCP) or
        Fluent Bit's <code>forward</code> output at port <code>24224</code>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 48px;">Good to know</h2>
      <ul style="line-height: 1.9;">
        <li><b>gRPC lands here.</b> Our API speaks OTLP/HTTP (JSON + protobuf); the collector is the supported bridge for gRPC exporters — which is most default SDK and collector setups.</li>
        <li><b>PAT stays out of your app envs.</b> Only the collector holds the credential; rotate it in one place.</li>
        <li><b>Resilience.</b> The collector's retry + sending queue buffer through a brief API blip and drain on recovery.</li>
        <li><b>Compression.</b> <code>compression: gzip</code> is in the config and our API decompresses natively — large log batches arrive at a small fraction of their raw size on the wire.</li>
        <li><b>Metric types.</b> Gauge and Sum (counter) metrics are ingested today; Histogram/Summary points are acknowledged-but-skipped and reported in the OTLP <code>partialSuccess</code> response (full histogram support is on the roadmap).</li>
        <li><b>AI-agent traces.</b> GenAI spans (<code>gen_ai.*</code>) flowing through this collector get the full treatment: searchable content, cost analytics, and the AI-agent security detection pack.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
